The `getNumberOfActiveConnections()` function provides a reliable way to retrieve the number of active connections at any given time. The code uses the Boost Asio library to handle network connections. For real-time purging, you may want to implement a separate routine that runs in a separate thread or asynchronously with a timer, ensuring that inactive connections older than 15 minutes are purged periodically.

This implementation provides a good starting point for your requirements and can be further optimized based on specific use cases and constraints."]

['```java
import java.io.File;
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.math.BigInteger;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Path;
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;
import java.util.concurrent.ProgressLogger;

public class FileHashUtil {
    private static final int PROGRESS_INTERVAL = 10 * (1024 * 1024); // 10MB

    public static BigInteger sha256(String filePath) {
        try {
            MessageDigest messageDigest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
            ProgressLogger progressLogger = new ProgressLogger((float) PROGRESS_INTERVAL, System.out);

            Path path = File.valueOf(filePath).toPath();
            Files.walkFileTree(path, (fileTree, fileBase, fileAttribute) -> {
                if (Files.isRegularFile(fileBase)) {
                    try (FileInputStream fileInputStream = new FileInputStream(fileBase.toString())) {
                        byte[] buffer = new byte[PROGRESS_INTERVAL];
                        int bytesRead;

                        while ((bytesRead = fileInputStream.read(buffer)) != -1) {
                            messageDigest.update(buffer, 0, bytesRead);
                            progressLogger.logProgress();
                        }
                    } catch (IOException e) {
                        System.err.println("Error reading file: " + fileBase.toString() + ". Error message: " + e.getMessage());
                    }
                }
                return FileVisitor.CONTINUE;
            });

            return new BigInteger(1, messageDigest.digest());
        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException | IOException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Error calculating SHA-256 hash.", e);
        }
    }

    private static class ProgressLogger implements FileVisitor<Path> {
        private final float interval;
        private long totalBytesRead = 0;
        private int progressInterval;

        public ProgressLogger(float interval, PrintStream out) {
            this.interval = interval;
            this.progressInterval = (int) Math.ceil((double) interval / 1024); // convert to KB for easier calculations
        }

        void logProgress() {
            totalBytesRead += progressInterval * 1024;
            if (totalBytesRead >= interval) {
                System.out.printf("%.2f%% complete\r", ((double) totalBytesRead / new File(filePath).length()) * 100);
                totalBytesRead = 0;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This code provides a method `sha256()` that calculates the SHA-256 hash of a given file path using an efficient streaming approach. The memory usage is minimized by reading and processing data in chunks (10MB by default). A progress logger is implemented to display the percentage of completion during long-running operations.

The `ProgressLogger` class implements the `FileVisitor<Path>` interface, allowing it to be used with the Java 7 `Files.walkFileTree()` method. The file tree walk is performed recursively and skipping directories.']

