```java
import java.util.*;
import java.time.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

interface DistributedCache<K, V> {
    void put(K key, V value);
    Optional<V> get(K key);
    void update(K key, V newValue);
    void removeByPayloadSize(double maxPayloadSize);
}

class LogEntry implements Comparable<LogEntry> {
    final long logId;
    final Instant timestamp;
    final String eventType;
    final int payloadSize;

    public LogEntry(long logId, Instant timestamp, String eventType, int payloadSize) {
        this.logId = logId;
        this.timestamp = timestamp;
        this.eventType = eventType;
        this.payloadSize = payloadSize;
    }

    @Override
    public int compareTo(LogEntry other) {
        return Long.compare(this.timestamp, other.timestamp); // Sort by timestamp in descending order
    }
}

class CacheImplementation implements DistributedCache<Long, Map.Entry<LogEntry, Integer>> {
    private final ConcurrentHashMap<Long, Deque<Map.Entry<LogEntry, Integer>>> cache;
    private final int maxCacheSize;
    private final ScheduledExecutorService scheduler;

    public CacheImplementation(int maxCacheSize, TimeUnit timeUnit) {
        this.cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
        this.maxCacheSize = maxCacheSize;
        this.scheduler = Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(1);
        scheduler.scheduleAtFixedRate(() -> cache.values().stream()
                .filter(d -> d.size() > maxCacheSize) // Filter out entries exceeding max size
                        .flatMap(Collection::stream) // Flatten the Deque
                        .forEach(entry -> entry.setValue(0)), // Reset access count to 0 for removal
                Duration.ofMinutes(1), Duration.ofMinutes(1)); // Prune every minute
    }

    @Override
    public void put(Long logId, Map.Entry<LogEntry, Integer> entry) {
        cache.computeIfAbsent(logId, k -> new ArrayDeque<>()).addLast(entry);
    }

    @Override
    public Optional<Map.Entry<LogEntry, Integer>> get(Long logId) {
        return cache.getOrDefault(logId, new ArrayDeque<>())
                .stream()
                .max(Comparator.comparing(e -> e.getValue())); // Find the entry with the highest access count
    }

    @Override
    public void update(Long logId, Map.Entry<LogEntry, Integer> newEntry) {
        cache.computeIfPresent(logId, (k, v) -> {
            v.removeIf(e -> e.getKey().getPayloadSize() > newEntry.getKey().getPayloadSize()); // Remove older entries with larger payload sizes
            v.addLast(newEntry);
            return v;
        });
    }

    @Override
    public void removeByPayloadSize(double maxPayloadSize) {
        cache.values().forEach(d -> d.removeIf(e -> e.getKey().getPayloadSize() > maxPayloadSize));
    }
}
```

In this solution, the `LogEntry` class represents a log entry with its attributes: log ID, timestamp, event type, and payload size. The `CacheImplementation` class implements the provided interface `DistributedCache` to manage the cache system as per the requirements. It uses a `ConcurrentHashMap` for storing log entries, and a scheduled executor service to prune the cache periodically based on payload size.

The `put`, `get`, `update`, and `removeByPayloadSize` methods from the interface are implemented in this class. Additionally, the trade-off between space and time complexity is managed by maintaining a fixed-size cache and prioritizing more frequently accessed logs for retention. The system can adapt dynamically to changing loads using the scheduled executor service to prune the cache periodically based on payload size.

To handle high-throughput scenarios, consider implementing multi-threading or sharding techniques, which would involve splitting the cache across multiple nodes in a distributed environment. Also, consider implementing network partition tolerance and node failure handling mechanisms to ensure data integrity and availability under such conditions.']

